worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_handler_rules.js"
  ceiling 802
  rationale "Browser interpreter for data/seed/handler-rules.lino (issue #1085 D1.3). JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (clarification, punctuation_only_prompt, ill_formed, physical_action_question, opinion_question (the handler-rules interpreter)), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. Ceiling moved to 694 for issue #1175 R3 (follow-up round, 2026-10-08): the rule interpreter reads the prior_turn condition and the clarification twin passes the dialogue history to it. Ceiling moved to 774 for issue #918 (2026-10-08, R914-6 minimal-core batch): the interpreter gained three domain-free primitives the native rule interpreter gained with it, the role_slot capture, the stable_id value and the evidence condition, plus the handlerRuleSetClaims probe; with them conversation_topic, source_refresh and source_conflict left their bespoke twins in formal_ai_worker_04.js, formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js and formal_ai_worker_code_plans.js (and their Rust functions) for seed rules, so the growth is generic machinery replacing three handlers, not regrowth. Ceiling moved to 802 the same day for the fourth issue #918 batch: the interpreter gained the quoted and network_snapshot values and intent templating, with which the network_query snapshot, concept introspection and user filter became seed rules in both runtimes; the browser twin gained the two branches it used to leave native."
